KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
static assertion failed
--
The front end answers __is_trivially_equality_comparable conservatively
false for classes (cpp11_builtin_is_trivially_equality_comparable covers the
non-class types).  clang++ 18 accepts this program (the built-in is
clang-only), and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
